	"about": "The blue-grey the app started with, and the palette most editors' dark themes are a version of. It began as IDEA's values and stayed only in shape: dark quiet chrome, one warm colour for keywords, green for text you wrote, blue for things that are called — while every value here is ours, the greys carrying a little more blue and the syntax hues pulled apart so keyword, type and call read as three colours rather than three shades. Its daylight half is not the dark one inverted: a light theme wants more contrast in the text and less in the surfaces, or every panel edge shouts. The terminal is Ghostty's sixteen on a deep blue, a shade off the editor's own so the pane still reads as a terminal.",
